  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<!--Do not edit this div tag.  It must surround the interaction block-->
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="9a0e8228-dbbc-42d4-9bc8-0ea042e64963"><problem><para>
      <para>1. The height of water in a bathtub, \(w\), is a function of time, \(t\). Let \(P\) represent this function. Height is measured in inches and time in minutes. </para>
      <para>What does each equation mean in this situation?</para>
      <para>\(P(0) = 0\)</para>
      </para></problem><solution><para>The bathtub starts out with no water.</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is the bathtub starts out with no water. </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
